<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — MorphoEval overall 81.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics whose analytic Holocene wavelength is 56.00 µm, with marine a=0.28 at 61.81 µm and benthic a=0.14 at 52.23 µm on the same dx. Gamma sweep Pearson r against analytic λ_c was 0.9973 with RMSE 4.28 µm. Equal diffusion decays. The growth GIF scores cv_sim_similarity 88.4 against the Krisp specimen. Two readouts are not yet trustworthy: nearest-bin radial FFT and a percentile darkness that sits at ~0.35 on both images. Overall 81.1/100 (faithfulness 78.7, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888, image/png, 544837 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2 (sha256 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2), spec_fingerprint 3db7c83138922a03aef82aaf803ecbe744b83029257f1146668b5acc01d7c2cb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 3db7c83138922a03aef82aaf803ecbe744b83029257f1146668b5acc01d7c2cb; artifact_sha256: 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a53e439d8af1eeb7..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=69b13a9c5037e468..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=6e834bc83f029f3b..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=bc4c0aa8b21f50ae...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Miller 2007: freshwater Kitlg expression is reduced relative to marine sticklebacks | Tapanes & Rennison 2024: melanophore density and lateral barring are separable traits; reconstructed_in_script: a, Du, Dv, gamma chosen so Holocene analytic λ_c = 56 µm | a = 0.28/0.20/0.14 is a Kitlg-direction knob, not a measured rate; transfer_boundary: Nakamasu 2009 is a zebrafish pigment-cell network, not a stickleback measurement; does_not_claim: That 56 µm was measured on the photograph | That the organ-scale bars are the critical mode k_c." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1. Replace the within-image percentile darkness with an absolute luminance threshold so specimen and render fractions are not forced near 0.35.",
        "remediation needed: R2. Replace nearest-bin radial FFT with parabolic sub-bin interpolation so nonlinear wavelengths are not quantized in ~5 µm steps.",
        "remediation needed: R3. Re-measure marine, Holocene and benthic peaks after that interpolation and state whether the saturated benthic pattern actually shortens.",
        "remediation needed: R4. Leave the posterior flank half out of the cosine fit; do not raise posterior r by fitting the test segment." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.11e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — Parameter expressivity: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "γ in {3,4,6,8,10} moves analytic and measured wavelength together (r = 0.9973) in the direction λ ∝ γ^(−1/2). Equal diffusion (Du = Dv) yields activator std ~0 against pattern std 0.81. The nonlinear marine/Holocene/benthic separation is compressed relative to the analytic 61.81 / 56.00 / 52.23 µm triple, and the sweep RMSE is 4.28 µm." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

